$ mp --help
A CLI tool for sending emails from Markdown drafts with YAML frontmatter

Usage: mp [OPTIONS] [FILE] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  send            Send a single approved email, or (with --invite) a calendar invitation
  send-approved   Send all approved emails in a directory
  list            List emails by status
  validate        Validate YAML frontmatter in files
  mark-approved   Mark an email as approved
  mark-draft      Demote an approved draft back to `draft` status (reverse of `mark-approved`)
  new             Create a new email draft from template
  reply           Create a reply draft from a received email
  forward         Forward an email to new recipients
  invite          RSVP to a received calendar invitation (iMIP REPLY over SMTP)
  list-mailboxes  List available IMAP mailboxes/folders
  fetch           Fetch emails from IMAP server
  sync            Sync local mailbox folders with IMAP server
  watch           Watch a mailbox for changes using IMAP IDLE
  archive         Archive an inbox email (server + local)
  delete          Delete an inbox email (server + local)
  open            Open an email's attachment in the default application
  save            Save an email's attachment(s) to a directory
  search          Search emails on the IMAP server
  config          Manage configuration
  contacts        Contact index operations
  calendar        Calendar / iMIP invite operations
  dump-keys       Dump the TUI key bindings from the single KEYMAP source of truth
  help            Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Arguments:
  [FILE]  File to preview (dry-run mode)

Options:
  -s, --signature <SIGNATURE>  Signature to use (overrides config default)
      --no-signature           Skip signature entirely
  -A, --account <ACCOUNT>      Account to use (default: first in config)
  -h, --help                   Print help
  -V, --version                Print version

$ mp send --help
Send a single approved email, or (with --invite) a calendar invitation

Usage: mp send [OPTIONS] [FILE]

Arguments:
  [FILE]  Path to the email draft file (omit when using --invite)

Options:
  -y, --yes                        Skip confirmation prompt
      --invite                     Send an iMIP calendar invitation (METHOD:REQUEST) instead of a draft. Attendees come from --to/--cc; the subject is used as the event summary. Requires --to, --start, --subject, and one of --end/--duration
      --to <TO>                    Invite recipient(s), comma-separated (invite mode; ATTENDEE + To)
      --cc <CC>                    Invite CC recipient(s), comma-separated (invite mode; ATTENDEE + Cc)
      --subject <SUBJECT>          Event subject / summary (invite mode)
      --start <START>              Event start. Local time (2026-07-20T14:00 or "2026-07-20 14:00") or RFC3339 with offset (2026-07-20T14:00:00+02:00, ...Z). Invite mode
      --end <END>                  Event end (same formats as --start). Provide this or --duration
      --duration <DURATION>        Event duration instead of --end: ISO8601 (PT1H30M) or short (1h30m)
      --location <LOCATION>        Optional event location (invite mode)
      --description <DESCRIPTION>  Optional event description / body (invite mode)
  -s, --signature <SIGNATURE>      Signature to use (overrides config default)
      --no-signature               Skip signature entirely
  -A, --account <ACCOUNT>          Account to use (default: first in config)
  -h, --help                       Print help

